      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you should be very worried and seek immediate medical attention rather than sleeping it off because Eliquis (apixaban) is a strong blood thinner that significantly increases the risk of severe internal bleeding or swelling from head trauma. Even without external bleeding, an internal head bleed like a subdural hematoma can be life-threatening and may not show obvious symptoms for hours or days. Please go to an emergency room or call emergency services right away so they can perform a CT scan to rule out dangerous bleeding. Do not take any more medication and do not try to rest through this, as a small internal bleed can become a big emergency quickly.",
